deep_analysis.adaptation_guide:
This commit refactors vLLM's weight-loading plumbing (vllm/model_executor/models/utils.py): (1) AutoWeightsLoader.__init__ drops the `skip_prefixes` and `skip_substrs` kwargs (module/param skipping is now done exclusively via a WeightsMapper whose maps use None values), (2) WeightsMapper.get_unstacked_mapper() is renamed to get_rename_mapper() and additionally strips None-valued mappings, and (3) load_weights() now always composes REMOVE_UNUSED_ROTARY_EMBEDS_MAPPER into the (now always-present) mapper.

vllm-ascend has exactly one breaking call site: vllm_ascend/models/deepseek_mtp.py:54 in AscendGlmMoeDsaForCausalLM.load_weights, which calls `AutoWeightsLoader(self, skip_prefixes=["rot."]).load_weights(weights)`. After this commit that raises TypeError (unexpected kwarg `skip_prefixes`). Fix by passing a mapper that drops the `rot.` prefix instead:

    def load_weights(self, weights):
        loader = AutoWeightsLoader(self)
        return loader.load_weights(
            weights, mapper=WeightsMapper(orig_to_new_prefix={"rot.": None})
        )

`WeightsMapper` is already imported in this file (line 9). The other AutoWeightsLoader users in vllm-ascend are unaffected: qwen3_dspark.py:125 (no kwargs) and minimax_m3/minimax_m3.py:1208 and minimax_m3/minimax_m3_vl.py:370 (no kwargs; pass mapper=self.hf_to_vllm_mapper explicitly). No vllm-ascend code calls get_unstacked_mapper()/get_rename_mapper() directly, and the quant-config `apply_vllm_mapper` overrides (modelslim_config.py, compressed_tensors_config.py) only receive the mapper from upstream interfaces.py, so they inherit the new semantics without changes. Ideally also add/extend a test (e.g. tests/ut/ or the DeepSeek MTP loading test) asserting GLM MoE DSA MTP weights load on Ascend after the change.
